<details><summary>Reveal the exact fiber theorem and proof idea</summary>
For a key $h$ and target $y$, the equality $T_h(m)=y$ holds exactly when $m_i+h_i\ge y$ for every $i$ and equality holds for at least one $i$. Necessity follows from the definition of a finite minimum. Conversely, the inequalities put the minimum above $y$, while the active equality puts it below $y$. Thus the fiber is a union of faces of a translated orthant.
</details>

